WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.032
This is a healthy back tooth in the lower jaw.

00:00:03.382 --> 00:00:06.219
Inside is the pulp: the nerve and blood vessels.

00:00:07.019 --> 00:00:10.795
Deep decay can reach the pulp. Germs get in, and the pulp can die.

00:00:11.595 --> 00:00:14.966
The germs spread out of the root tips, and the bone there wears away.

00:00:15.766 --> 00:00:19.777
Pus can drain through a thin channel to the gum. It may hurt only a little.

00:00:20.577 --> 00:00:24.834
Root canal treatment cleans and seals the canals. Then the bone can heal,

00:00:24.834 --> 00:00:26.059
over months or years.
